            "text": "Synthetic Identity Fraud (SIF) involves blending real and fabricated data to create hybrid identities that mimic legitimate users. Fraudsters exploit data breaches, generate synthetic documents via AI, and layer identities across institutions to evade detection. SIF also involves creating interconnected profiles with subtle shared attributes (e.g., phone numbers, email domains) and atypical feature combinations (e.g., unusual age-to-income ratios, abnormal geolocation patterns). Fraudsters operate through networks of profiles, leveraging AI to mimic legitimate behavior.",
